// Korean. Like ja, zhHans and id, Korean does not inflect nouns for
// number, so every plural family here is .other only -- the buckets the
// plural resolver actually reads for this language.
//
// Register is the plain 해요체 the interface wants, not the stiffer 합니다체.
// The audio loanwords a Korean musician already uses (보컬, 드럼, 베이스,
// 루프) stay loanwords; translating those would read as odd to anyone who
// has opened a DAW.
